{"id":"n-20261019-33s9gx","category":"sports","display_title":"Pep Guardiola Releases Video Supporting UNRWA","display_title_he":"פפ גווארדיולה פרסם סרטון תמיכה באונר\"א","short_summary":"Football manager Pep Guardiola has released a video condemning Israel's military actions and calling for international funding and solidarity for UNRWA.","english_level":"C1","words":518,"reading_time":4,"image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/54/Pep_Guardiola_reacting_to_the_UCL_draw_Man_City_vs_Real_Madrid_2025.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","credit":"SportsMax TV · CC BY 3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pep_Guardiola_reacting_to_the_UCL_draw_Man_City_vs_Real_Madrid_2025.jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"Ynet","domain":"ynet.co.il","url":"https://www.ynet.co.il/sport/worldsoccer/article/ryno2ex2ze","title":"גווארדיולה ממשיך במתקפה נגד ישראל: \"רצחה עשרות אלפי בני אדם בעזה\"","published_at":"2026-10-19T03:30:00.000Z"},{"name":"Walla","domain":"sports.walla.co.il","url":"https://sports.walla.co.il/item/3872772","title":"גווארדיולה שוב תוקף: \"ישראל רצחה עשרות אלפי בני אדם בעזה\"","published_at":"2026-10-19T00:13:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-19T00:13:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-19T06:21:25.216Z","quality_score":8,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["In a newly released public video, football manager Pep Guardiola has voiced vehement criticism of Israeli military actions in the Gaza Strip while calling for urgent international backing for the United Nations Relief and Works Agency for Palestine Refugees (UNRWA). Running for just over three minutes, the recording features the former Manchester City manager appealing directly to audiences worldwide, urging them to donate to the UN agency and sustain active humanitarian assistance for the Palestinian population.","Throughout his address, Guardiola focused intensely on civilian distress, concentrating particularly on the plight of children and the immense human toll of the war. Rejecting clinical descriptions of conflict casualties, he emphasized that individuals killed in the hostilities must not be regarded as mere statistics or dismissive collateral damage. He argued that accepting sanitized language conceals suffering and strips humanity of its moral compass. According to Guardiola, children are enduring catastrophic conditions—searching desperately through rubble for missing parents, crying out for assistance, confronting severe starvation, and facing utter abandonment before having any chance to experience adulthood. He asserted that the pain felt by Palestinians is not alien and should command equal consideration.","Directing explicit accusations toward Israeli authorities, Guardiola stated that the Israeli government has murdered over thirty-four thousand people in Gaza and continues to obstruct the delivery of essential humanitarian aid. He maintained that global solidarity cannot take an intermission, emphasizing an enduring collective responsibility to advocate for civilian protection. Beyond Gaza, Guardiola also touched upon the West Bank, where he contended that home demolitions and the forced displacement of Palestinian residents persist unabated.","A substantial portion of the message was devoted to highlighting the enduring mission of UNRWA, which has provided medical care, protection, and vital humanitarian relief to Palestinian refugees for more than seventy-five years. Guardiola described the organization as far more than an operational relief channel, characterizing it as a vital archive of historical memory. In his assessment, UNRWA preserves the identity, rights, and legacy of successive generations of Palestinian refugees, serving as living proof that their existence cannot be erased.","Concluding his appeal, the Spanish coach warned that allowing destruction to persist relies upon enforced silence, insisting that staying quiet represents an implicit choice to take a side. He urged observers not to avert their gaze, describing the ongoing conflict as one of the darkest periods in contemporary history. He implored members of the global public to resist pervasive apathy, continue speaking out about Palestine, and provide direct financial backing to UNRWA so the agency can continue delivering aid to those in deepest distress.","This recorded message forms part of a consistent pattern of public interventions by Guardiola regarding the war. Last year, he reflected on four-year-old children killed by bombs or dying in failing hospitals, warning that people must not dismiss these horrors as someone else's problem, because the next young victims could easily be their own. Furthermore, after wearing a keffiyeh at a Barcelona charity gathering and labeling the hostilities in Gaza as genocide during a Manchester press briefing, Guardiola affirmed his firm resolve to utilize his global platform whenever he can offer assistance."],"facts":[{"fact":"Pep Guardiola appeared in a video lasting slightly over three minutes supporting UNRWA and criticizing Israel's conduct in the Gaza war.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Guardiola accused the Israeli government of having murdered over 34,000 people in Gaza and continuing to obstruct humanitarian aid.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"In the video, Guardiola stated that civilian casualties are not numbers or collateral damage, highlighting children suffering starvation, searching rubble for parents, and being left alone.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Guardiola highlighted UNRWA's role over more than 75 years in providing healthcare, protection, and aid, calling it an institution preserving Palestinian refugee identity and memory.","sources":[2]},{"fact":"Guardiola touched upon home demolitions and forced displacement in the West Bank.","sources":[2]},{"fact":"Guardiola previously called events in Gaza a genocide, wore a keffiyeh at a Barcelona 